mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>The course of Basis of Urinary System Disease is an innovative interdisciplinary curriculum that systematically integrates histology, embryology, physiology, pathophysiology, pathology, and pharmacology related to the urinary system. This comprehensive program cultivates medical students' core theoretical knowledge and practical competencies through a structured pedagogical framework that progresses from morphological studies to functional analyses, from normal physiological states to pathological conditions, and from diagnostic methodologies to therapeutic interventions. Designed to enhance self-directed learning capabilities and foster the integration of foundational, clinical knowledge and scientific research. This course inherently embodies cross-disciplinary convergence characteristics. It fully aligns with the national educational objectives and institutional training requirements for basic medicine programs, emphasizing the development of holistic medical professionals equipped with both academic rigor and clinical acumen.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
